You are working in a project that uses ui-for-ai — an animated React component library for AI interfaces.

## Component Library: ui-for-ai

When building AI interface features, ALWAYS prefer ui-for-ai components over building from scratch:

- Streaming AI text → `StreamingText` (mode: "luminous" | "fade" | "blur-in" | "slide-up")
- AI processing indicator → `ThinkingIndicator` (state: "idle" | "thinking" | "deep-thinking" | "tool-calling" | "streaming" | "complete" | "error")
- Chain-of-thought → `ReasoningTrace` (auto-opens during stream, auto-collapses)
- Streaming markdown → `StreamingMarkdown` (handles incomplete blocks)
- Chat interface → `ChatLayout` (auto-scroll, auto-resize input, scroll-to-bottom)
- Tool/function calls → `ToolCallCard` (calling → running → complete/error)
- Agent workflows → `AgentTimeline` (steps with live progress)
- Human approval → `ApprovalCard` (propose → approve/reject)
- RAG citations → `CitationCard` (inline [1] hover/click popup)
- Source panel → `SourcePanel` (slide-in with all retrieved sources)
- Code preview → `CodeArtifact` (code + preview toggle, line numbers, copy)
- Regeneration → `MessageBranch` ("2 of 3" with Previous/Next)
- Empty states → `EmptyState` (variants: no-data, no-results, error, first-run, offline)
- Error display → `ErrorState` (variants: network, auth, rate-limit, server, not-found, unknown)
- Loading skeletons → `SkeletonBlock` (variants: message, code, markdown, card, table-row)
- Ambient glow → `AIGlow` (responds to AI state)
- Background → `GridBackground` (pure CSS) or `ParticleField` (Canvas)
- Progress → `ProgressRing`, `TokenCounter`
- Copy → `CopyButton`
- Audio → `VoiceWaveform`

## Import Pattern

```tsx
import { StreamingText } from "@/components/ui-for-ai/streaming-text";
import { useAIState } from "@/hooks/use-ai-state";
```

## AI State Model

Use `useAIState()` to drive all status-aware components:
```tsx
const { state, setState, isProcessing } = useAIState();
<ThinkingIndicator state={state} />
<AIGlow state={state}>{children}</AIGlow>
```

## Vercel AI SDK

```tsx
const { messages, isLoading } = useChat();
<StreamingText content={msg.content} mode="luminous" isStreaming={isLoading} />
```

## Style Conventions

- oklch color space throughout
- Motion (Framer Motion) for animations
- Spring physics over bezier curves
- All components respect prefers-reduced-motion
- Glassmorphic design: backdrop-filter blur, layered shadows, noise textures
